const GLOSSARY = [
 ["Regular season","The 82 games each team plays from October to April. The results decide who makes the playoffs."],
 ["Conference","A large group of teams inside a league, usually East and West. In the NBA each has 15 teams, and teams compete for position inside their own conference."],
 ["Seed","A team's rank in its conference. The No. 1 seed is the best, and higher seeds get more home games in the playoffs."],
 ["Playoffs","The knockout tournament after the regular season that decides the champion. In the NBA and NHL, a team must win four rounds."],
 ["Play-In","A short tournament for seeds 7 to 10 in each conference. Two of the four move on to the playoffs."],
 ["Best-of-seven","A playoff series: the first team to win four games advances."],
 ["Draft","Each June, teams take turns picking new players. The weakest teams usually pick first, which is how bad teams get better."],
 ["Lottery","The draw that sets the draft order among teams that missed the playoffs."],
 ["Trade","Teams swap players or future draft picks."],
 ["Free agent","A player whose contract has ended and who can sign with any team."],
 ["Salary cap","A limit on what each team can spend on players, so the richest teams cannot simply buy everyone."],
 ["Rebuild","When a team gives up on winning now, trades veterans for young players and picks, and builds for the future."],
 ["Contender","A team good enough to win the championship this season."],
 ["Rookie","A player in their first season."],
 ["MVP","Most Valuable Player: the award for the best player of the regular season."],
 ["Triple-double","Reaching double figures in three stats in one game, usually points, rebounds and assists."],
 ["Net rating","Points scored minus points allowed per 100 possessions. A quick way to see how good a team really is."],
 ["Pace","How many possessions a team plays per game. Higher means faster."],
 ["Rivalry","Two teams with history, usually from playoff battles or sharing a city. Rivalry games feel bigger."],
 ["Bandwagon","Picking up a team when it starts winning. Long-time fans may tease you. You are welcome anyway."]
];

